From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:00:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 29/46] Touch input on the canvas on Android

One finger is the left mouse button: its press waits until the finger
moves past a small slop, lifts (a click) or rests 120 ms, so that a second
finger can still turn the touch into a gesture.  Two fingers pan and pinch-
zoom about their midpoint.  A quick three-finger tap zooms to fit.

The mouse events are injected through QWindowSystemInterface (kiplatform
InjectTouchMouse), so capture, button state and the reported pointer
position follow them as for a real mouse.  Qt's pan and pinch recognisers
are not used on Android: once Qt has made the first finger a mouse drag, a
second finger never reaches the canvas.  The Vulkan canvas window now
forwards touch to the canvas widget, which accepts touch, instead of its
viewport.

